From: Joel Groves <happygreentreefrog@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: find the 802.11 header behind EHT radiotap TLVs

mt76_connac3_mac_decode_eht_radiotap() pushes the EHT and U-SIG radiotap
TLVs in front of the 802.11 header and sets RX_FLAG_RADIOTAP_TLV_AT_END,
leaving mac_header pointing at the header. mt76_skb_get_hdr() only skips
the HE radiotap structs, so for EHT frames it returns the first TLV.
The TLV type (0x0021) then reads as the frame control of a management
frame without ToDS.

mt76_check_ccmp_pn() therefore checks every EHT-received data frame
against the robust management frame replay counter instead of the
per-TID one. Frames from different TIDs share one PN counter, and
whenever a lower-priority TID is delivered after a higher one with a
newer PN, its frames are marked RX_FLAG_ONLY_MONITOR and disappear
without any counter. On a BT8 6 GHz EHT mesh this lost 30-60% of the
rear-to-house traffic; a diagnostic build showed 3778 PN check failures
in 60 s, all in the management slot (security_idx 16) for aggregated
data frames.

Return mac_header when the TLVs are present. Use the same header
pointer for the A-MSDU first subframe check, which also assumed the
header starts at skb->data.

---
diff --git a/mac80211.c b/mac80211.c
index eaaefb6..802f7ca 100644
--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -901,7 +901,10 @@ static void mt76_rx_release_amsdu(struct mt76_phy *phy, enum mt76_rxq_id q)
 		int offset = 0;
 
 		if (!(status->flag & RX_FLAG_8023)) {
-			offset = ieee80211_get_hdrlen_from_skb(skb);
+			struct ieee80211_hdr *hdr = mt76_skb_get_hdr(skb);
+
+			offset = (u8 *)hdr - skb->data +
+				 ieee80211_hdrlen(hdr->frame_control);
 
 			if ((status->flag &
 			     (RX_FLAG_DECRYPTED | RX_FLAG_IV_STRIPPED)) ==
diff --git a/mt76.h b/mt76.h
index 563dfc7..631cb6e 100644
--- a/mt76.h
+++ b/mt76.h
@@ -1463,6 +1463,12 @@ static inline void *mt76_skb_get_hdr(struct sk_buff *skb)
 
 	mstat = *((struct mt76_rx_status *)skb->cb);
 
+	/* EHT radiotap TLVs are pushed in front of the 802.11 header and
+	 * mac_header is left pointing at the header itself.
+	 */
+	if (mstat.flag & RX_FLAG_RADIOTAP_TLV_AT_END)
+		return skb_mac_header(skb);
+
 	if (mstat.flag & RX_FLAG_RADIOTAP_HE)
 		data += sizeof(struct ieee80211_radiotap_he);
 	if (mstat.flag & RX_FLAG_RADIOTAP_HE_MU)
